      "image": null,
      "state": {}
     },
     {
      "kicker": "01 · The line",
      "title": "Cut by hand, <em>line by line.</em>",
      "body": "Every line here was left standing by a woodcutter's knife; everything else was cut away. Watch them return in the order your eye finds them.",
      "fact": "Pear wood block, about 21 × 30 cm. Printed in thousands of copies.",
      "at": null,
      "length": 2.2,
      "intro": false,
      "hint": null,
      "place": null,
      "surface": null,
      "button": null,
      "image": null,
      "state": {}
     },
     {
      "kicker": "02 · The ink",
      "title": "Armour that <em>wasn't there.</em>",
      "body": "Dürer gave it plates like a suit of armour, a scaly hide and a small extra horn on its back. None of them are real, and almost everyone believed them anyway.",
      "fact": "Even school textbooks used Dürer's rhinoceros until the 1930s.",
      "at": null,
      "length": 1.6,
      "intro": false,
      "hint": null,
      "place": null,
      "surface": null,
      "button": null,
      "image": null,
      "state": {}
     },
